/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (Software development is the systematic process of conceiving, designing, coding, testing, and deploying computer applications that fulfil specific functional requirements. Over the past several decades, this process has evolved considerably, shifting from purely manual, code- intensive practices toward increasingly automated and visual methods of application building. This evolution has been driven by the growing demand for faster delivery of digital solutions, the shortage of skilled programmers relative to business needs, and the increasing complexity of enterprise requirements. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
