/E (Traditional coding refers to the conventional method of software development in which a programmer writes source code line-by-line using a programming language such as Java, Python, C++, or JavaScript. This method follows the well-established phases of the Software Development Life Cycle \(SDLC\), including requirement analysis, system design, implementation, testing, deployment, and maintenance. Traditional coding offers complete control over application logic, architecture, and performance, making it the preferred choice for building complex, large-scale, and performance-critical systems. However, it requires significant technical expertise, longer development timelines, and higher project costs. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (In contrast, low-code development is a modern software engineering paradigm that enables the creation of applications through visual interfaces, drag-and-drop components, and configuration-based logic, thereby minimizing the amount of hand-written code required. Low- code platforms abstract much of the underlying programming complexity, allowing both professional developers and citizen developers to build functional applications rapidly. This approach has gained substantial popularity in recent years due to its ability to accelerate digital transformation initiatives, reduce dependency on specialized programming skills, and lower overall development costs, while still enabling integration with existing enterprise systems. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (Several factors have contributed to the rising adoption of low-code platforms, including the increasing pace of business change, the need for rapid prototyping, a persistent shortage of experienced software developers, and the growing emphasis on empowering business users to participate directly in application development. Industry research organizations such as Gartner and Forrester have consistently reported strong year-on-year growth in the low-code application platform market, reflecting its expanding role in enterprise software strategy. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (Zoho Creator is a widely used low-code application development platform offered by Zoho Corporation. It enables users to design, build, and deploy custom business applications using a visual builder, pre-built templates, and its proprietary scripting language known as Deluge \(Data Enriched Language for the Universal Grid Environment\). Zoho Creator supports database management, workflow automation, third-party integrations, and multi-device deployment, making it suitable for building internal business tools, process automation systems, and departmental applications without extensive programming effort. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (The purpose of this comparative study is to critically examine and evaluate the Traditional Coding Method and the Zoho Creator Low-Code Platform across various technical, economic, and operational parameters. This experiment aims to provide a clear understanding of the )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
