121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (Traditional coding operates on the principle of explicit instruction, where the developer defines every logical step, control structure, and data operation required for the application to function correctly. The source code is written according to the syntax rules of the chosen programming language, compiled or interpreted into executable form, and then tested to verify correct behavior against the specified requirements. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (Traditional coding is the conventional approach to software development in which programmers write, compile, and execute source code manually using high-level or low-level programming languages to implement the desired functionality of an application. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (The development process involves writing modular code, designing database schemas, implementing business logic, creating user interfaces, integrating external APIs, and conducting rigorous testing. Version control systems and collaborative development tools are typically used to manage code changes among development teams. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
