/P 67 0 R
/E (Traditional coding strictly follows the phases of the SDLC: requirement gathering and analysis, system design, implementation \(coding\), integration and testing, deployment, and maintenance. Each phase is executed sequentially or iteratively, depending on the chosen process model such as Waterfall, Agile, or Spiral, and requires significant coordination among developers, testers, and project stakeholders. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
